      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.agents%2Fskills%2Fgenerate-profile%2FSKILL.md",
      "changes": 7,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/.agents%2Fskills%2Fgenerate-profile%2FSKILL.md?ref=13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5",
      "deletions": 3,
      "filename": ".agents/skills/generate-profile/SKILL.md",
      "patch": "@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ This skill launches an SGLang server, validates it with a quick accuracy test, g\n \n - A working SGLang installation (`pip install -e .` or equivalent)\n - At least one available CUDA GPU\n+- The `sgl-eval` CLI, installed in its own virtualenv as described in `.claude/rules/prefer-sgl-eval.md`, not in the server's env\n \n ## Step-by-step Workflow\n \n@@ -49,7 +50,7 @@ Typical startup time: 30-90 seconds depending on model size and whether CUDA gra\n sgl-eval run gsm8k --base-url http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1 --num-examples 20\n ```\n \n-- Expected accuracy: **> 0.8** for capable models (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, etc.)\n+- Expected `score`: **> 80%** for capable models (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, etc.)\n - This is a quick sanity check, not a rigorous benchmark.\n - If accuracy is unexpectedly low, something is wrong — do not proceed to profiling.\n \n@@ -108,8 +109,8 @@ for i in $(seq 1 120); do\n done\n \n # 3. Accuracy check\n-python3 -m sglang.test.run_eval --host 127.0.0.1 --port 30000 --eval-name gsm8k --num-examples 20\n-# Expected: Accuracy > 0.8\n+sgl-eval run gsm8k --base-url http://127.0.0.1:30000/v1 --num-examples 20\n+# Expected: score > 80%\n \n # 4. Profile\n python3 -m sglang.test.send_one --profile",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.agents%2Fskills%2Fgenerate-profile%2FSKILL.md",
      "sha": "bc22fd5e0b11073bf7d2ca145a900173cc813d25",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.agents%2Fskills%2Fwrite-sglang-test%2FSKILL.md",
      "changes": 4,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/.agents%2Fskills%2Fwrite-sglang-test%2FSKILL.md?ref=13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": ".agents/skills/write-sglang-test/SKILL.md",
      "patch": "@@ -388,9 +388,9 @@ A `register_*_ci(...)` under `python/sglang/` is rejected by the\n \n ## Eval Accuracy Mixins\n \n-**Design philosophy**: Most test files don't care about eval logic — they only need a \"does this feature break model output quality?\" sanity check. The mixin pattern separates **what to test** (threshold) from **how to test** (run_eval, assertions, CI summary). Test classes declare thresholds as class attributes; the mixin provides the `test_*` method. Override when you need extra assertions (e.g. EAGLE accept length).\n+**Design philosophy**: Most test files don't care about eval logic — they only need a \"does this feature break model output quality?\" sanity check. The mixin pattern separates **what to test** (threshold) from **how to test** (the eval call, assertions, CI summary). Test classes declare thresholds as class attributes; the mixin provides the `test_*` method. Override when you need extra assertions (e.g. EAGLE accept length).\n \n-Available mixins in `python/sglang/test/kits/eval_accuracy_kit.py`: `MMLUMixin`, `HumanEvalMixin`, `MGSMEnMixin`, `GSM8KMixin`. Can be combined freely. Read the source for attrs and defaults.\n+Available mixins in `python/sglang/test/kits/eval_accuracy_kit.py`: `MMLUMixin`, `HumanEvalMixin`, `MGSMEnMixin`, `GSM8KMixin`. Can be combined freely. Read the source for attrs and defaults. `MMLUMixin` already scores through sgl-eval; `GSM8KMixin` still defaults to the deprecated `run_eval` backend for existing tests, so new tests set `gsm8k_backend = \"sgl_eval\"`. The exception is a base or completion-only model: sgl-eval only sends chat requests, so those stay on the 5-shot completion backend.\n \n ```python\n class TestMyFeature(CustomTestCase, MMLUMixin):",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.agents%2Fskills%2Fwrite-sglang-test%2FSKILL.md",
      "sha": "f4a6293aacabc4dd3001167404f397252b352a40",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 31,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.claude%2Frules%2Fprefer-sgl-eval.md",
      "changes": 31,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/.claude%2Frules%2Fprefer-sgl-eval.md?ref=13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": ".claude/rules/prefer-sgl-eval.md",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+# Accuracy evals: use sgl-eval\n+\n+Use [sgl-eval](https://github.com/sgl-project/sgl-eval) whenever you measure a\n+model's accuracy.\n+\n+- **Against a server:** run the `sgl-eval` CLI from its own virtualenv, not the\n+  server's env, at the version pinned in the `test` extra of\n+  `python/pyproject.toml`.\n+\n+  ```bash\n+  sgl-eval run gsm8k --base-url http://127.0.0.1:30000/v1 --num-examples 200\n+  ```\n+\n+- **In a test:** use `sglang.test.sgl_eval_utils.run_sgl_eval` or the kits\n+  that wrap it. A new `GSM8KMixin` test sets `gsm8k_backend = \"sgl_eval\"`.\n+\n+- **Sampling:** use the model's recommended settings (temperature, top_p,\n+  thinking, max tokens) unless the user says otherwise. sgl-eval overrides\n+  them with its own defaults, so pass them explicitly, or use\n+  `--load-preset-from-model-id` when the model has a preset. `--thinking` only\n+  sets the `thinking` chat-template key; if the model's template reads a\n+  different one (commonly `enable_thinking`), pass that key with\n+  `--chat-template-kwarg` instead. When comparing against a CI test, use that\n+  test's settings (printed in its log as `sgl-eval <name> generation: {...}`).\n+\n+Do not use the deprecated `sglang.test.run_eval` or `few_shot_gsm8k`, `lm-eval`,\n+or a hand-written scorer. The exceptions are evals sgl-eval doesn't ship, and\n+base models, since sgl-eval only sends chat requests.\n+\n+Only compare scores from the same harness and settings, and say which ones you\n+used when you report a number.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/.claude%2Frules%2Fprefer-sgl-eval.md",
      "sha": "19993e87e0a5f450ae4c43af847218dfe9eee53c",
      "status": "added"
    },
    {
      "additions": 3,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/python%2Fsglang%2Ftest%2Ffew_shot_gsm8k.py",
      "changes": 7,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Ftest%2Ffew_shot_gsm8k.py?ref=13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5",
      "deletions": 4,
      "filename": "python/sglang/test/few_shot_gsm8k.py",
      "patch": "@@ -2,9 +2,8 @@\n Run few-shot GSM-8K evaluation.\n \n .. deprecated::\n-    This module is deprecated. Use ``sglang.test.run_eval`` with\n-    ``eval_name=\"gsm8k\"`` instead, which routes through the unified\n-    Chat API evaluation framework with dump_metric support.\n+    This module is deprecated. Use ``sgl-eval run gsm8k`` or\n+    ``sglang.test.sgl_eval_utils.run_sgl_eval`` instead.\n \n Usage:\n python3 -m sglang.test.few_shot_gsm8k --num-questions 200\n@@ -58,7 +57,7 @@ def get_answer_value(answer_str):\n def run_eval(args):\n     warnings.warn(\n         \"sglang.test.few_shot_gsm8k is deprecated. \"\n-        \"Use sglang.test.run_eval with eval_name='gsm8k' instead.\",\n+        \"Use `sgl-eval run gsm8k` or sglang.test.sgl_eval_utils.run_sgl_eval instead.\",\n         DeprecationWarning,\n         stacklevel=2,\n     )",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/13d1ab46283ec5f4f07e62ea8575be87b40859e5/python%2Fsglang%2Ftest%2Ffew_shot_gsm8k.py",
